  "sourceFindings": [
    "The public slip applied-template action binding points change to common$IChangeTemplateUserAction; it is not the configuration create/modify handler.",
    "ChangeTemplateUserAction records per-slip template changes in page runtime and current template in page state, then reloads with preserved template. For by_slip and multiple data_sids it confirms all/current; the cancel branch applies only current instead of cancelling all selection changes. This does not prove the complete resolver or persistent-default server behavior.",
    "The shared current-template reader validates a previous template_set_sid against the template_list and otherwise reads default_template from menu metadata for tenant/business/menu/type. The writer and precedence between company/user/menu defaults remain outside this scope.",
    "The sales-status FAQ uses conditional-form exception true-result and optional ID/device conditions for next entry default. This example is not the exact020 purchase print-default manual.",
    "A separate official FAQ explicitly supports per-form shrink default for purchase-order printing through detailed print settings; operating own page options lack that setting."
  ],
